{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the whole congregation of the children of Israel came.</b> This teaches that not a single person was missing from them." "<b>On the fifteenth day of the second month.</b> We take it that Rosh Chodesh Nisan, on which Israel went out of Egypt, was the fifth day of the week. If so, the fifteenth of Iyyar, on which they came to the wilderness of Sin, was the day of Shabbat, and they complained against Moses, and he said to them: 'in the evening you shall eat meat, and in the morning the manna will come down.' This follows the one who says: on Shabbat I assigned the boundariy marks, I did not assign them — therefore they were not strict to journey on it."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:06.846345959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}